# Touch Switch PCB

A capacitive touch-activated switch implemented using a 555 timer to toggle an output when a touch input is detected.

## Overview
This project demonstrates a simple human-interface circuit where touch input changes the capacitance at the trigger node, causing the circuit to activate an output indicator.

## Key Features
- Capacitive touch input pad
- NE555 timer-based control logic
- LED and buzzer output indicators
- Operates on 5 V DC
- Simple and intuitive user interaction

## How It Works
Touching the input pad alters the capacitance at the trigger pin of the 555 timer, changing its state and activating the output indicators.

